    "title": "Tidy loose fibres",
    "text": "With small fabric scissors, carefully trim only loose lint and frayed tips around the tear on the outside. Leave stable fabric and the remaining cross-threads. Work away from fingers and close scissors after. Done when no loose balls stick up but the hole size is unchanged.",
